			<div class="content" id="post-content-1903638">
									

<p>Minor grammatical issues:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Really&nbsp;minor</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Really&nbsp;minor</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1544's exterior is a mobile, 1 meter tall multicolored skin covering. It is 1 meter in height, and is controlled by a small, peach colored mass located in the center.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You're repeating the height in two sentences. Break it down to one: SCP-1544 is 1 meter in height and has a mobile multi-colored skin covering controlled by a small peach-colored mass located in the center.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>However, SCP-1544 will hibernate at temperatures exceeding 85° C, to preserve energy and prevent its interior from overheating.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Remove the second comma.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1544 will not return to it's usual behavior until music is played once more.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>its, not it's. And &quot;once more&quot; isn't quite right tone-wise. Maybe &quot;until music recommences&quot;?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>3. SCP-1544 has been proven to be able to consume plant life, though it will often throw the food through it's hands with what has been confirmed to be stomach bile.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>its, not it's.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>It just needs a bit of tightening up and fixing the grammar errors, but oh, poor Dr. Wondertainment. He just wants his buddy to be treated nice!</p>

